<h2 class="mb-3">Background</h2>

<p>
    Originally housed in a modest reading room near the Gampola railway station,
    the library was formalised under the Urban Council in 1959 and earned Grade I
    status in July 1994—one of only a handful of libraries in the Kandy District to
    achieve this distinction.
</p>

<p>
    Major milestones include the opening of a purpose‑built two‑storey facility in
    2002, the launch of the Children’s Wing in 2012, and our selection in 2021 for
    the national <em>Digital Libraries Project</em>, which introduced KOHA automation,
    high‑speed internet and an Online Public Access Catalogue (OPAC).
</p>

<p>
    In 2025 we rolled out this new Library Management System to streamline
    circulation, RFID self‑check, SMS/e‑mail notices and analytics—laying the
    groundwork for smart‑library services well into the future.
</p>

